# clang-tidy config — the static-analysis CI leg (test-hardening row 9).
#
# Defect-class checks only: the compiler's own diagnostics, the clang static
# analyzer, and the bugprone/performance/portability groups. Style and
# modernization (readability-*, modernize-*) stay OFF — formatting and API
# conventions are not this gate's job. bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters is
# an API-design opinion, excluded with the style class; the rest of bugprone-*
# and clang-analyzer-* is exactly the "syntax/obvious-defect" surface the leg
# exists for. Enforcement is warn-level with a baseline (see
# tools/static-analysis/clang-tidy.sh) — this file only scopes the check set.
#
# Header scope is pinned at the invocation (--header-filter, anchored to
# src/dsh_*.h): vendored engine trees are upstream, not ours to gate (D6).
Checks: >
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
FormatStyle: none
